{"aggregate_id": "01KTKSFTZ3HMJDS73FPREW38NY", "aggregate_type": "Mission", "event_id": "01KTKSFV4ABWC2EWFZMPS122FD", "event_type": "MissionCreated", "payload": {"created_at": "2026-06-08T14:16:51.941907+00:00", "friendly_name": "Vikunja client + habits weekly report", "mission_id": "01KTKSFTZ3HMJDS73FPREW38NY", "mission_number": null, "mission_slug": "vikunja-client-and-habits-weekly-report-01KTKSFT", "mission_type": "software-dev", "purpose_context": "Mission delivers the bundled #562/#542/#561 slice: (1) a new scripts/common/vikunja_client.py (foundation per #542); (2) a new scripts/habits/query_active_habits_weekly.py deterministic helper plus migration of scripts/habits/query_active_habits_v2.py to the client; (3) output-discipline Hard Rules in felix-admin-habits/AGENTS.md mirroring capture's pattern (per #561), plus audit of felix-admin-escalation and felix-admin-tasker for the same gap; (4) agent prompt rewiring so the weekly cron invokes the helper instead of hallucinating data. Recurrence-aware scheduling uses Vikunja's native repeat_after + repeat_mode encoding per memory reference_vikunja_recurrence_model.md.", "purpose_tldr": "Make the weekly habit report trustworthy by replacing LLM improvisation with a deterministic helper, building it on a shared Vikunja client that future scripts also use, and adding output-discipline Hard Rules so the agent stops leaking internal reasoning to WhatsApp.", "target_branch": "main", "wp_count": 0}, "project_slug": "kg-automation", "project_uuid": "2c011d09-8272-470c-b9e2-e9ccf8ad3fbd", "schema_version": "5.0.0", "timestamp": "2026-06-08T14:16:52.106202+00:00"}
